quran[28]{c,v,t}:
  69,35,"So today, he has no loyal friend here,"
  69,36,"nor any food except filthy pus,"
  69,37,which none shall eat except the evildoers.’
  69,38,"So I swear by whatever you see,"
  69,39,and whatever you do not see.
  69,40,"Indeed, this (Qur’an) is the word spoken by a Noble Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him)."
  69,41,And it is not the word of a poet (as you claim). How little do you believe!
  69,42,Nor is it the word of a fortune-teller. How little do you reflect!
  69,43,(It is) a revelation gradually sent down from the Lord of all worlds.
  69,44,"Had he fabricated any sayings about Us,"
  69,45,"We would have surely seized him by the right hand,"
  69,46,and then cut off his aorta.
  69,47,Then none of you could have shielded him (from Us).
  69,48,"Indeed, this (Qur’an) is a reminder for the God-conscious."
  69,49,And We certainly know that some of you are (its) deniers.
  69,50,"Indeed, it will be a (matter of) regret for the disbelievers."
  69,51,"But most surely, it is the Certain Truth."
  69,52,"So glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most Magnificent."
  70,1,"A questioner asked about the punishment bound to occur,"
  70,2,"upon the disbelievers, which none can repel,"
  70,3,"from Allah, Lord of the Ascending Ways."
  70,4,The angels and the Spirit ascend to Him in a Day whose span is fifty thousand (earthly) years.
  70,5,So endure with graceful patience.
  70,6,"Indeed, they think this (Day) to be distant,"
  70,7,but We see it as near.
  70,8,"On that Day, the sky will be like molten copper,"
  70,9,and the mountains like (flakes of) coloured wool.
  70,10,"And no close friend will ask about his friend,"
